# repo-scan-public-addresses — mail addresses and Message-IDs that upstream has
# already published, which devtools/repo-scan therefore lets through (BRIEF §7,
# "What upstream has already published is public"; operator, 2026-10-13).
#
#   @host      every address at exactly that host. ONLY for mailing-list hosts,
#              where every address is a public list. Never an organisation's
#              or a mail provider's domain: that would also pass addresses
#              nobody published.
#   token      one address or one whole Message-ID, matched exactly.
#
# Add an entry when a public upstream record (a lore or patchwork mail, a commit
# trailer, a stable review) carries it, with a comment saying which. Never add a
# private correspondent. The project author's own address is allowed by
# repo-scan already (and so are vger.kernel.org, lists.linux.dev, kernel.org).

